<BRK/></SPT>
]</SPT>]</TAI><TAI OPT="NAVFAC PAC,NORFOLK NAVAL SHIPYARD">[<SPT><TTL>Restrictions on Use of Yellow[, Orange-Yellow, Red, and Magenta] Materials</TTL><BRK/>
<TAI OPT="NORFOLK NAVAL SHIPYARD"><NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  Add the following for projects at Norfolk Naval Shipyard (NNSY).  This paragraph is tailored for NNSY.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
[<TXT>Refrain from use of yellow or orange-yellow materials for the following purposes:  sheeting, tarpaulins, polyethylene bottles or other containers, 
tapes, bags, banding of identification marks on tools, boundary markers such as ribbons.  Contractor generated yellow waste materials such as torn 
foul weather gear must be disposed of by the Contractor off-yard.  Shipyard dumpsters and trash cans must not be used for disposal of Contractor 
generated yellow waste materials.  Yellow colored items such as described above are of specific significance within the shipyard and are subject 
to strict controls.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
]</TAI><TAI OPT="NAVFAC PAC"><NTE><AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  Add the following for shipyard projects at NAVFAC PAC.  This paragraph is tailored for NAVFAC PAC.</NPR><BRK/>
