   </TDA>
</WBK>
<BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/></TAB><BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>Contractor Berthing Facilities (CBF)</TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  Check with the Public Works Office at U.S. Naval Base Guantanamo Bay, Cuba to determine where Contractor 
employees will be berthed and if berthing is available.  Use this paragraph for Contractor Berthing Facilities 
(CBF) requirements.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<TXT>For this task order, the Government will supply the number of ESBF beds for the period of time as supported by the Contractor's personnel-loaded 
CPM schedule provided in Section <SRF>01 32 17.00 20</SRF> COST-LOADED NETWORK ANALYSIS SCHEDULE (NAS).  Except for allowed fair market rental units (Family/Management 
Quarters) Contractor employees (unaccompanied status) will be berthing with the Navy Exchange, Navy Gateway Inns and Suites Division (NGIS) in 
ESBF located on both sides of the bay; Windward (WW) and Leeward (LW).  ESBF primarily consists of multi-occupancy rooms with wither shared or 
gang head bathrooms.  Due to the configuration of most facilities, they are not suitable for mixing genders; therefore, female residents are not 
accepted by NGIS for occupancy in ESBF.  Provide alternate berthing for all female employees.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>Pricing</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Costs are based on occupied beds.  The current rate is $15.00 per person per bed, regardless of room configurations with the exception of suites 
located at Building AV640 which are $30.00.  Rates are reviewed each March for implementation each October.  Should prices increase, the Contractor 
will receive, at a minimum, 30 days notification.  Bed night costs are not negotiable.</TXT><BRK/>
<OLG><BRK/>
<OLI>Utility Rates:  In addition to the rates for berthing, the utility rate of $8.52 per day per person will apply, regardless of room configuration.  
Rates may be adjusted each Fiscal Year.  This rate will be billed separately.  Any price increases [and][or] decreases to CBF and utility 
rates/costs will not be subject to economic price adjustment(s) and any increases [and][or] decreases to these areas of Contractor overhead 
will not be considered and reimbursed pursuant to the changes and disputes clauses to this contract.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>At no additional cost to the Government, the Contractor must provide temporary housing for their unaccompanied employees who do not qualify 
for CBF or if CBF is full.  For transient lodging information or to make reservations contact the NGIS by e-mail at ngis.gtmo.reservation@navweb.org, 
by phone at 757-458-2044 or by visiting their main office located at Building 1670.  Current transient rates as of June 2023 range from 
$60.00 to $90.00 depending on room configuration and location.</OLI><BRK/></OLG>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>Billing</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Contractors will be billed monthly for the number of beds assigned to their company.  Contractors are charged for beds assigned to employees on 
leave unless the employee removed all personal property and checks out of the facility.  Remit payment on or before due dates.  Administrative 
and late fees apply.  Failure to promptly pay can result in eviction from the premises regardless of impact to Contractor ability perform the contract 
specifications.  NGIS makes no guarantee of bed availability or berthing locations.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>Contractor Berthing Agreement</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Prior to berthing any employees, complete a Contractor Berthing Agreement with the NGIS.  A copy of this agreement is available at the NGIS management 
offices located at Building 1670.  To determine availability, advance registration and notification of berthing requirements is highly recommended; 
send information via e-mail to NGIS mail box at <URL HREF="ngis.gtmo.reservation@navweb.org">ngis.gtmo.reservation@navweb.org</URL>.  Allow 5-10 days for responses.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
</SPT></SPT></SPT></TAI><TAI OPT="ARMY"><SPT><TTL>ARMY AND ARMY NATIONAL GUARD REQUIREMENTS AND RESTRICTIONS</TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  This paragraph is tailored for ARMY.  Use for projects on Army and Army National Guard installations.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL><SUB>3Rs Explosive Safety Education Training Certificate</SUB></TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>All Contractor and subcontractor employees requiring access to Army or Army National Guard installations, facilities, and areas for the performance 
of a contract or subcontract must complete the 3Rs (Recognize, Retreat, Report) Explosives Safety Education Program training.  Complete the training 
within 30 calendar days after the date of receipt of a written notice of award.  The Contractor is responsible for ensuring that all subcontractor 
employees complete the training before access to the installation is required for performance of the subcontract.  The Contractor is also responsible 
for ensuring that all contractor and subcontractor employees renew the training annually for the duration of the performance period of the contract 
or subcontract.  Submit certificates of completion for each Contractor and subcontractor employee subject to this requirement to the Contracting 
Officer’s Representative (COR) or to the Contracting Officer, if a COR is not assigned, within 5 calendar days after completion of training.  3Rs 
Explosives Safety Education Program training is available at the following website: <URL HREF="https://www.denix.osd.mil/uxo/3rs-training">https://www.denix.osd.mil/uxo/3rs-training/</URL>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
</SPT></TAI></PRT><PRT><TTL>PART 2   PRODUCTS</TTL><NED/><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Not used.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></PRT>
<PRT><TTL>PART 3   EXECUTION</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Not used.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></PRT>
    <END/><BRK/></SEC>